# ICPay Trade — Plan 2: Swap migration (Motoko → Rust)

**Status:** design only  
**Date:** August 2026  
**Decision:** **Yes** — move all swap logic to a Rust `icpay_trade` canister and **delete** Motoko `SwapService`.  
**Trade canister = swap** (v1). Trading UI + limits come later (plan1 extras).

**Fee:** **0.1%** of swap amount (10 bps) — **not** flat 0.1 ICP.  
**Speed target:** **official ICPSwap `depositFromAndSwap`** — 1 pool call per trade (not 3).

---

## 0. Fee model — 0.1% (not flat ICP)

| | Today (Motoko) | Trade (new) |
|---|----------------|-------------|
| Service fee | **0.1 ICP flat** (`10_000_000` e8s) | **0.1%** of `amount_in` |
| Config | `SWAP_ICP_SERVICE_FEE_E8S` | `SERVICE_FEE_BPS = 10` |
| Small swap (1 ICP) | User pays 0.1 ICP (~10%) | User pays 0.001 ICP |
| Large swap (100 ICP) | User pays 0.1 ICP (~0.1%) | User pays 0.1 ICP (~0.1%) |
| Break-even | ~100 ICP swap | — |

### How fee is collected (clean + fast)

```rust
// domain/fees.rs — pure, unit-tested
pub const SERVICE_FEE_BPS: u64 = 10; // 0.1%

pub fn service_fee(amount_in: u64) -> u64 {
    amount_in.saturating_mul(SERVICE_FEE_BPS) / 10_000
}

pub fn swap_amount_after_fee(amount_in: u64) -> u64 {
    amount_in.saturating_sub(service_fee(amount_in))
}
```

**Skim from `token_in`** before pool call — accrue fee on trade main, batch to treasury hourly:

```
amount_in (user trading balance)
  → service_fee (0.1%) accrue on trade main (0 IC writes)
  → depositFromAndSwap(remainder) → output to trade canister
  → credit user trade balance (internal, 0 IC writes)
```

| Swap type | Old (flat ICP fee) | New (0.1%) |
|-----------|-------------------|------------|
| ICP → ckBTC | Separate ICP transfer to treasury **+** swap | Skim 0.1% from ICP input — **one less hop** when batched |
| ckBTC → ICP | Needs ICP balance for 0.1 ICP fee | Fee taken from ckBTC input — **no ICP required** |

**Quote must show:** `service_fee`, `amount_in`, `amount_after_fee`, `amount_out`.

**Minimum fee:** `1` unit (1 e8s) floor so dust swaps don’t round to zero.

**Treasury sweep (optional v2.1):** accrue fees on trade main, `heartbeat` transfers to treasury hourly — **0 extra writes per swap**.

---

## 1. Recommendation (short)

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| Write swap in Rust trade canister? | **Yes** |
| Remove from Motoko wallet? | **Yes**, after parity + mainnet soak |
| Better than keeping Motoko swap? | **Yes** — isolation, **~5× fewer cycles**, **0.1% fee**, ICPSwap one-step |
| Touch bucket / transfer / community? | **No** — wallet unchanged except thin fund bridge |
| One feature or two? | **One** — “swap” is the trade canister; `/swap` redirects to `/trade` |

---

## 2. Before vs after

```
BEFORE (today)
  Frontend /swap
       → icp_wallet_backend (Motoko)
            SwapService.mo  (920 lines + SwapStorage + api/v1/Swap.mo)
            + custody + bucket + community + …

AFTER (target)
  Frontend /trade  (v1: same swap UI, v2: terminal)
       → icpay_trade (Rust)     ← ALL ICPSwap + swap state
       → icp_wallet_backend      ← custody ONLY
            depositToTrade / withdrawFromTrade  (2 thin endpoints)
```

**Wallet never calls ICPSwap again.**

---

## 3. What we delete from Motoko (checklist)

| File / area | Action |
|-------------|--------|
| `src/services/SwapService.mo` | **Delete** |
| `src/storage/SwapStorage.mo` | **Delete** |
| `src/api/v1/Swap.mo` | **Delete** |
| `main.mo` swap wiring + `SwapService.create` | **Remove** |
| `testing/swap/*.test.mo` | **Move** → `trade/tests/` (PocketIC) |
| `testing/services/SwapService.test.mo` | **Replace** with Rust unit tests |
| `Config.mo` `ICPSWAP_*`, `RATE_SWAP` | **Move** to trade canister config |
| `types.mo` `SwapQuoteResult`, `SwapResult` | **Remove** from wallet; live in trade `.did` |
| `#swapIn` / `#swapOut` tx types | **Keep** on wallet only if we still mirror one line in tx history (optional); else trade owns history |

**Keep on wallet:** everything else (transfer, withdraw, deposit, bucket, community, username, admin).

---

## 4. Rust trade canister — clean module layout

Single responsibility: **ICPSwap execution + swap/trade state**.

```
trade/
├── Cargo.toml
├── trade_canister.did
└── src/
    ├── lib.rs                 # init, post_upgrade, export_candid!, timers
    ├── config.rs              # factory id, fee tiers, service fee, wallet id
    ├── types.rs               # ApiResult, Quote, SwapResult, Order (later)
    │
    ├── api/                   # thin #[query] / #[update] — no business logic
    │   ├── quote.rs           # get_swap_quote
    │   ├── swap.rs            # execute_swap, recover_failed_swap
    │   └── balance.rs         # (v2) trade balance read
    │
    ├── domain/                # pure logic — unit tested, no ic_cdk
    │   ├── quote.rs           # fee math, min_out, slippage
    │   ├── swap.rs            # validation, balance checks
    │   └── fees.rs
    │
    ├── storage/               # ic-stable-structures
    │   ├── pools.rs           # pair → pool id cache
    │   ├── escrows.rs         # failed swap recovery (replaces SwapStorage)
    │   ├── balances.rs        # (v2) per-user trade balance
    │   └── history.rs         # swap tx log for UI
    │
    ├── icpswap/               # external actors only
    │   ├── factory.rs
    │   └── pool.rs            # quote, deposit_from, swap, withdraw
    │
    ├── ledger/
    │   └── icrc.rs            # transfer, approve, fee
    │
    └── wallet/
        └── gate.rs            # verify caller == WALLET for credit/debit
```

**Rules (same as `backend/.agents/skills/rust/SKILL.md`):**

- `api/` → delegate only  
- `domain/` → testable, no `ic_cdk`  
- Max **~300 lines** per file  
- Return `ApiResult<T>`, never trap on user input  

---

## 5. Candid API — v1 swap parity

Match current frontend needs first; rename later if needed.

```candid
type ApiResult = variant { Ok : SwapResult; Err : text };

type SwapQuoteResult = record {
  amount_out : nat;
  amount_out_raw : nat;
  service_fee : nat;
  amount_after_fee : nat;
  swap_fee : nat;
  price_impact : text;
  pool_id : text;
};

type SwapResult = record {
  block_index : nat64;
  amount_in : nat;
  amount_out : nat;
  service_fee : nat;
  tx_id : text;
};

// --- queries (free) ---
get_swap_quote : (token_in : text, token_out : text, amount_in : nat) -> (variant { Ok : SwapQuoteResult; Err : text }) query;

// --- user updates ---
execute_swap : (token_in : text, token_out : text, amount_in : nat, amount_out_min : nat) -> (ApiResult);
recover_failed_swap_input : (token_in : text, token_out : text, amount_in : nat) -> (variant { Ok : nat; Err : text });

// --- wallet-only (v1 fund bridge) ---
credit_from_wallet : (user : principal, token : text, amount : nat, block_index : nat64) -> (variant { ok; err : text });
debit_to_wallet : (user : principal, token : text, amount : nat) -> (variant { Ok : nat64; Err : text });
```

**Wallet adds (Motoko, ~50 lines total):**

```motoko
depositForSwap : (ledgerId : Text, amount : Nat) -> async ApiResult<Nat>;
// transfer sub → trade canister + credit_from_wallet

withdrawFromTrade : (ledgerId : Text, amount : Nat) -> async ApiResult<Nat>;
// debit_to_wallet + transfer to user sub
```

---

## 6. Official ICPSwap integration (clean)

Source: [ICPSwap-Labs/docs](https://github.com/ICPSwap-Labs/docs)

| Canister | Principal | Use |
|----------|-----------|-----|
| **SwapFactory** | `4mmnk-kiaaa-aaaag-qbllq-cai` | `getPool` (query) — fee tiers 500 / 3000 / 10000 |
| **SwapPool** | per pair | `quote` (query), **`depositFromAndSwap`** (update) |
| **Token ledgers** | ICRC | `icrc2_approve` once per token |

### What Motoko does wrong today

Uses the **3-step** manual flow from older guides:

```
depositFrom → swap → withdraw   (3 pool updates)
```

Plus wallet hops + separate ICP fee transfer = **7 writes total**.

### What we use instead (official one-step)

From [Executing DepositFromAndSwap](https://github.com/ICPSwap-Labs/docs/blob/main/02.SwapPool/Swap/04.Executing_DepositFromAndSwap.md):

```candid
type DepositAndSwapArgs = record {
  amountIn : text;
  zeroForOne : bool;
  amountOutMinimum : text;
  tokenInFee : nat;
  tokenOutFee : nat;
};

depositFromAndSwap : (DepositAndSwapArgs) -> (variant { ok : nat; err : Error });
```

**One pool update** = deposit + swap + withdraw output **directly to caller** (trade canister).

### Rust pool actor (minimal — only what we need)

```rust
// icpswap/pool.rs — match deployed ICPSwap v3, nothing extra

#[derive(CandidType)]
struct DepositAndSwapArgs {
    amount_in: String,
    zero_for_one: bool,
    amount_out_minimum: String,
    token_in_fee: u64,
    token_out_fee: u64,
}

trait SwapPool {
    async fn quote(&self, args: SwapArgs) -> Result<u64, PoolError>;
    async fn deposit_from_and_swap(&self, args: DepositAndSwapArgs) -> Result<u64, PoolError>;
    async fn get_user_unused_balance(&self, user: Principal) -> Result<(u64, u64), PoolError>;
}
```

**Do not implement:** mint, liquidity, limit orders on pool until M6.  
**Quote:** `factory.getPool` (query) → `pool.quote` (query) — both free.

### Token standard labels (must match factory)

| Token | `standard` field |
|-------|------------------|
| ICP | `"ICP"` |
| ckBTC, ckETH, ckUSDC, ckUSDT | `"ICRC2"` |
| SNS / other ICRC-1 | `"ICRC1"` |

---

## 7. Execution path — optimal (one pool call)

### Why not “instant”?

| Layer | Limit |
|-------|--------|
| IC consensus | **~2–4s per update** |
| Minimum swaps | **1 pool update** with `depositFromAndSwap` |
| **Hard floor** | **~2–5s** after approve is warm |

### Best path (v1 — ship this)

```
ONE-TIME per token:
  depositForSwap(amount)           // wallet → trade main
  icrc2_approve(pool, allowance)   // once per token/pool

EVERY swap (~2–5s, 1 pool write):
  execute_swap:
    fee = 0.1% of amount_in        // accrue on trade main (0 writes)
  pool.depositFromAndSwap({
    amountIn, zeroForOne, amountOutMinimum,
    tokenInFee, tokenOutFee
  })
    → output lands on trade canister
  credit user trading balance      // StableBTreeMap (0 writes)
```

```
┌─────────────┐  deposit once   ┌──────────────────┐
│ Wallet      │ ───────────────► │ Trading balance   │
│ subaccount  │ ◄─────────────── │ (per-user ledger) │
└─────────────┘  withdraw       └────────┬─────────┘
                                           │
         depositFromAndSwap (1 IC write)   ▼
                                    ICPSwap pool
```

### Writes per repeat swap

| Step | IC write? | Cycles (est.) |
|------|-----------|---------------|
| Wallet deposit | Once per top-up | ~47M |
| `icrc2_approve` | Once per token | ~40M |
| Service fee 0.1% | **No** (accrue) | 0 |
| **`depositFromAndSwap`** | **Yes** | ~40M |
| User balance credit | **No** (stable map) | ~0 |
| Treasury sweep | Hourly timer | amortized |

**Repeat swap (warm approve): ~47M cycles, ~2–5s**  
**vs Motoko today: ~280M cycles, ~15–35s** → **~6× fewer cycles, ~4× faster**

If approve expired: +40M (~87M total).

### Stuck funds recovery (official)

Query `getUserUnusedBalance(trade_canister_principal)` on pool.  
If non-zero after failed swap → `withdraw` to trade main → credit user.  
Port as `recover_failed_swap` — same idea as today’s Motoko escrow.

